{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1542530-1e-supernatural-npcs-stats","id":1542530,"title":"1e Supernatural NPCs Stats","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-09-23T12:21:18-07:00","id":1542530,"title":"1e Supernatural NPCs Stats","content":"I saw that in the 2e books like Changeling and Geist are missing the rules to make True Fae and a Deathlord. In case of entities such as these, where 2e didn't adjourned the specific rules for stats, are the ones that are in the 1e books still valid barring specific powers like Contracts for the True Fae?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28580-madoglio14","name":"Madoglio14","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-23T12:54:08-07:00","id":1542531,"title":"","content":"The rules for creating True Fae is on pages 169-170 in Changeling: The Lost Second Edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-23T13:39:56-07:00","id":1542532,"title":"","content":"The deathlords never had stats in 1e (they're plot device-tier characters) and are not referenced at all in 2e, but if you feel like statting one up the material in Imperial Mysteries for modeling Rank 6+ entities should translate fairly directly to 2e, given that the Manifestation system specifically doesn't apply to entities of that scale, who instead rely on purely narrative criteria of the sort that would take the length of one or more stories to come to pass in order for them to leave their home dimensions (in this case the Underworld, where the main Rank 5 and 6 beings are Kerberoi who start suffering Essence Bleed as soon as they leave their own Dominions).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-25T13:37:17-07:00","id":1542638,"title":"","content":"Regarding the deathlords from Sarchel, i meant the Kerberoi that in the first edition of Geist are not the Deathlords and they are described as another type of entities","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28580-madoglio14","name":"Madoglio14","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-25T20:14:59-07:00","id":1542660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madoglio14</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1542530-1e-supernatural-npcs-stats?p=1542638#post1542638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the deathlords from Sarchel, i meant the Kerberoi that in the first edition of Geist are not the Deathlords and they are described as another type of entities</div> </div> </div> </div>The Deathlords mentioned in 1e have never in any official book for either edition been given any stats or even definition as to what they are. If anything in 2e corresponds to 1e's Deathlords, it's what 2e calls the Chthonic Gods. The Chthonic Gods also are never given any stats or clear definition, and a sidebar questions whether they even exist as a separate entity from the general goings on of the Underworld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-25T21:17:53-07:00","id":1542664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madoglio14</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1542530-1e-supernatural-npcs-stats?p=1542638#post1542638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the deathlords from Sarchel, i meant the Kerberoi that in the first edition of Geist are not the Deathlords and they are described as another type of entities</div> </div> </div> </div>General mechanics for the Kerberoi in 2e are on pages 197-198 of Geist 2e Core as part of the larger section on unusual ghosts and chthonians, as well as on pages 232-233 in the Antagonists chapter; apart from those additions, they're modeled as Rank 5 or 6 ghosts, the latter of which are treated as plot devices by most characters for the purposes of conflict resolution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}